      "ImageDescription": {
        "value": "A traditional Finnish midsummer bonfire being burned in the Suomenlinna islands off the southern coast of Helsinki, Finland. Midsummer 2014 was an exceptionally cool midsummer in the entire southern Finland. Only the bonfire kept me warm during the entire day. Only less than a month afterwards, in middle July, the weather in Finland was so warm I had to stop wearing a jacket and only wear a T-shirt on my upper body.",
